@title STORY • LONDON: THE MEAN TWIN
@bg penthouse_morning
You're London Sterling. You wake up at 5:15 so you can be "four minutes early." You've been late every day this season on purpose. Showing up early would mean admitting you care.
Your phone: Dr. Ames. "Reminder: Thursday 4pm."
Your phone: Mama. "Proud of you baby. Every single day."
You've been in recovery since fourteen. Some mornings it's background noise. Some mornings it's the loudest thing in the room. Today it's quiet. You'll take quiet.
> [Good] Text Mama back: "love you. going to my appointment thursday." -> a1
> [Sweet] Wake Paris up and make her eat breakfast with you. -> a2
*a1
@add Recovery 2
Mama: "❤️❤️❤️ that's my girl"
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Paris_Bond 3
Paris: (half asleep, at the counter) You're being weird. Nice-weird.
London: Eat your eggs, Paris.
It's the best part of your morning. You'll never tell her that.
*a_done
@bg track_stadium_morning
@show diggy
Diggy is already on the track. He's always already on the track. You've checked. Every day. You'd rather die than let anyone know you've checked.
@show cassie
Cassie: (sliding up) You're staring.
London: I'm surveying.
Cassie: You're surveying Diggy's calves.
> [Bitchy] "I'm surveying the TRACK, Cassie." -> b1
> [Bold] "And? They're objectively good calves." -> b2
> [Sweet] Walk away before your face gives you up. -> b3
*b1
Cassie: The track is behind you.
London turns around. The track is, in fact, behind her.
@jump b_done
*b2
@add Honest 2
Cassie: (screaming into her own hands) I'm TELLING MAGGIE.
London: Maggie already knows.
Cassie: EVERYONE already knows.
@jump b_done
*b3
@add Diggy_Crush 1
You walk away fast. Too fast. Diggy calls "morning, Sterling!" and you trip on absolutely nothing.
*b_done
@bg penthouse_night
That night, alone on the balcony, you write in the journal Dr. Ames made you start. "Three true things."
> [Sweet] 1. I like him. 2. I'm scared. 3. I'm okay. -> c1
> [Bitchy] 1. He's annoying. 2. He's annoying. 3. ...He's annoying. -> c2
> [Good] 1. I ate breakfast with my sister. 2. I ran well. 3. I'm proud of me. -> c3
*c1
@add Honest 3
You stare at number one. You don't cross it out. That's new.
@jump end
*c2
You close the journal. You open it again. Under number three, very small, you write "(I like him.)"
@jump end
*c3
@add Recovery 3
Dr. Ames would say that's the most important page you've written. You think she'd be right.
*end
London Sterling is mean, sharp and impossible to impress. She's also the girl who checks every morning if he's on the track, and who's getting better, one quiet morning at a time.
